# Moku: local development settings. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in what you need.
#
# Who reads this file:
#   - The brain of a development build: scripts/build-app.sh links build/.env to this repository's .env and tells the
#     app where it is (MokuDevEnv), and the brain reads it (brain-go/internal/brain/env.go). It takes JEV_VERCEL,
#     MOKU_GATEWAY_URL, MOKU_ACCESS_TOKEN and MOKU_* keys from it, only those not already set in the environment or in
#     ~/.moku/credentials.env.
#   - A brain run by hand (`go run .` in brain-go/) reads the environment and ~/.moku/credentials.env instead; point it
#     at this file with MOKU_DEV_ENV=/path/to/.env.
# Release builds never read it.

# --- Model access for the brain (pick one) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# With neither, a development build gets a trial token from the relay on its first launch, like any new Mac, and
# without any access the brain decides by its rules alone.

# A) Your own Vercel AI Gateway key. Jev (judging) and Luna (names and short lines) are called directly, with zero
#    data retention.
JEV_VERCEL=

# B) Your own relay (proxy/), with a token it issued. The gateway key then stays on the relay.
# MOKU_GATEWAY_URL=https://<your-relay>.vercel.app/v4/ai
# MOKU_ACCESS_TOKEN=moku_...

# Other models, for experiments (the defaults shown).
# MOKU_MODEL_JUDGE=typesafe-ai/jev
# MOKU_MODEL_WRITER=openai/gpt-6-luna

# --- The brain (all optional) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOKU_HOME=~/.moku              # the database, config, credentials and logs
# MOKU_BRAIN_PORT=8020           # 127.0.0.1 only
# MOKU_LOCAL_MODEL=off           # never download or run the local fallback model
# MOKU_GOAL_JUDGING=1            # experimental goal-aware judging (docs/rules.md)

# --- Building (scripts/build-app.sh, scripts/release.sh, app/MokuVisual/scripts/run-demo.sh) ---------------------
# MOKU_VERSION=0.1.0                                       # the app's version
# MOKU_LOCAL_MODEL=0                                       # leave the llama.cpp server out of the app (releases do)
# MOKU_UPDATES_URL=https://<your-relay>.vercel.app/updates   # releases only: the update feed's base address
# MOKU_SIGNING_IDENTITY=                                   # run-demo.sh only; default: ad hoc ("-")
